<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Redirect Mapper — Match Old URLs to New URLs for a Site Move</h1>
    <p>Paste your old URLs and your new URLs and this <strong>free redirect mapper</strong> matches each old page to its closest new page, flags weak matches and chains, and gives you ready-to-paste 301 rules for Apache or Nginx plus a CSV. No signup, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="rm-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Redirect mapper form">
        <div>
          <label for="rm-old">Old URLs (one per line)</label>
          <textarea id="rm-old" style="min-height: 170px;" placeholder="https://old-site.com/services/seo-audit.html&#10;https://old-site.com/blog/2019/link-building-tips&#10;https://old-site.com/about-us"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="rm-new">New URLs (one per line)</label>
          <textarea id="rm-new" style="min-height: 170px;" placeholder="https://new-site.com/services/seo-audit/&#10;https://new-site.com/blog/link-building-tips/&#10;https://new-site.com/about/"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="rm-format">Output format</label>
          <select id="rm-format">
            <option value="report">Match report</option>
            <option value="apache">Apache (.htaccess) 301 rules</option>
            <option value="nginx">Nginx 301 rules</option>
            <option value="csv">CSV preview</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong>Redirect map</strong>
        <span id="rm-status" class="llms-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Waiting for input</span>
      </div>
      <pre id="rm-output" class="llms-output" style="max-height:420px;white-space:pre-wrap;">Paste old and new URLs to build the map.</pre>
      <div class="llms-actions" style="margin-top:14px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="rm-copy">Copy</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-glass" id="rm-csv">Download CSV</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>How the Matching Works</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>Path clean-up first.</strong> Each URL is reduced to its path. The domain, query string, fragment, letter case, trailing slash and common extensions such as <code>.html</code> and <code>.php</code> are ignored.</li>
      <li><strong>Same path.</strong> If an old path appears unchanged in the new list, it is an exact match and scores 100.</li>
      <li><strong>Same page name, new folder.</strong> When the last part of the path is identical but the folder changed, the match is strong.</li>
      <li><strong>Word overlap.</strong> Otherwise the tool compares the words in the two paths, ignoring common filler words, and picks the new URL with the highest overlap.</li>
      <li><strong>Three outcomes.</strong> A strong match is marked <em>Match</em>, a partial one is marked <em>Review</em>, and anything weaker is marked <em>No match</em> so you decide it by hand instead of sending it somewhere irrelevant.</li>
      <li><strong>Chain and merge warnings.</strong> The tool flags a target that is itself an old URL, which would create a redirect chain, and counts how many old pages point at the same new page.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What a Redirect Map Is For</h2>
    <p>When URLs change, a redirect map says which new page each old page should send visitors and search engines to. Google distinguishes between permanent and temporary redirects: with a permanent redirect it treats the new target as the canonical page, while a temporary one can leave the old page in results. For a site move it recommends permanent server-side redirects wherever possible.</p>
    <p>Google's site move guidance also says not to send many old URLs to one irrelevant destination such as the new homepage, which can be treated as a soft 404, and to keep redirects for as long as possible, generally at least a year. That is why this tool leaves weak matches unmatched instead of filling every row.</p>
    <p>The matching uses words in the URL only. It does not read your pages, so it cannot tell whether two pages cover the same topic. Treat the result as a first draft, check every Review and No match row, and test a sample of the final redirects before launch.</p>

    <h2>Redirect Mapper FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Does the mapper look at the content of my pages?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. It compares only the words in the URLs you paste, so it cannot see page content or intent. Review the weaker matches against the actual pages.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which redirect type do the rules use?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>301, a permanent redirect, which is what Google recommends for a permanent move. Change the code yourself if you need a temporary redirect.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why are some old URLs left unmatched?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No new URL shared enough words with them. Redirecting them to an unrelated page, especially the homepage, is discouraged, so they are listed for you to map by hand or retire.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can several old URLs point to one new URL?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes, when old pages were merged into one. The tool counts these so you can confirm that the merge was intended.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my URLs anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. The matching runs in your browser with JavaScript — nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Planning a site move or redesign?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix maps URLs, checks redirects and monitors indexing through the move.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

